# SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
#
# Test-only relaxations. Everything else is inherited from the repository root,
# so tests are held to the same standard as the library except where a check
# cannot see through the test framework.
#
# -bugprone-unchecked-optional-access: Catch2's REQUIRE is opaque to the
#   checker, so `REQUIRE(x.has_value()); use(*x);` -- the correct and idiomatic
#   way to assert on an optional -- is reported as unchecked. In test code the
#   check produces only false positives, and the alternative is either dozens of
#   NOLINT comments or contorting assertions to satisfy a tool. It remains
#   enabled for src/ and include/, where it earned its place: it caught a real
#   readability problem in src/cbor/reader.cpp, where failure recording relied
#   on a postcondition the reader had to take on trust.
---
InheritParentConfig: true
Checks: '-bugprone-unchecked-optional-access'
